  "origin": {
    "kind": "new",
    "note": "Written for live-mix on cpp/kit. A two-segment digital waveguide string (Karplus-Strong and Jaffe-Smith lineage) with the excitation at the junction. The ebow and the bow share one driver: it reads the string's own fundamental, pushes in phase with it to hold a set level, and adds upper partials from a table read at the string's phase (the octave for a hard-driven ebow, a slipping-string ramp plus rosin noise for the bow). A friction-junction bow was tried and dropped because it fell into double-slip and whistling regimes. Not a model of a particular instrument."
  }
